# =============================================================================
# PixelArt Creator — generated .gitignore
# Layered per orchestrator-design `references/project-structure.md` §5.
# Layers (a)-(d) are the constant doctrine; layer (e) is this project's stack.
#
# NOTE: under the container standard (project-structure.md §1) the orchestration
# system lives OUTSIDE this repository, beside it in the container:
#     PixelArt-Creator/            <- container (not a repo)
#     |-- .claude/  memory/  scripts/  (+ a private documentation folder)
#     |-- CLAUDE.md  STRUCTURE.md  DEPLOYMENT.md  constitution.md
#     `-- main/                    <- THIS REPOSITORY
# The layer (a) entries below are belt-and-suspenders for any session launched
# inside this folder, where a stray write would otherwise land in the repo.
# =============================================================================

# ---- (a) AI-constitution and system files -----------------------------------
constitution.md
DEPLOYMENT.md
STRUCTURE.md
ROADMAP.md
design-docs/
.claude/

# ---- (a2) the orchestration system's half of this repository's own store ----
# `memory/` as a whole was class (a) while this repository had no store. It
# has one now, and a repository that ignores its whole store commits NO map:
# the Repo and History views come up empty on any clone and store-role.json is
# invisible to everyone but the machine that created it. Only the SEMANTIC
# half stays out — lessons belong to the orchestration system and reach the
# container's store through promotion on merge.
memory/insight/
memory/cards/
memory/promotions.jsonl
memory/archive/

# ---- (b) Agent artifacts ----------------------------------------------------
subagent-report-*.md
checkpoint-*.md
claude-checkpoint-*.md
gather-*
loop-state-*.json
swarm-state-*.json
*.superseded
dev-docs/

# ---- (c) Memory-graph derived files (rebuildable from the JSONL logs) -------
memory/graph/index.db
memory/graph/index.db-wal
memory/graph/index.db-shm
memory/graph/scan-state.json

# ---- (d) Tooling and caches -------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
node_modules/
.claude/worktrees/
coverage/

# ---- (e) Python / PySide6 stack ---------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode & extensions
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Packaging / build
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
wheels/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Native-installer / local-CI build byproducts (pyside6-deploy + Nuitka)
/dist/
/build/
*.dist/
*.build/
*.onefile-build/
deployment.qmake
.nuitka/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Test / coverage / type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
*.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/

# testing/ own runner artefacts (N-4b): the Coverage frame's source
# artefact changes on every run, so a clone that has never run the
# suite has measured nothing, which is what the frame then reports.
# .coverage / .coverage.* / *.coverage above already reach
# testing/.coverage and its parallel-mode fragments (unanchored
# patterns match at any depth); coverage.json is a distinct filename
# those patterns do not cover.
testing/coverage.json
# The portable default temp root testing/run and run.cmd fall back to
# when $ORCH_TEST_TMP is unset (never a literal drive letter in either
# wrapper - kept portable rather than hardcoding a drive letter).
.tmp/

# ---- Editors / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- PixelArt Creator runtime scratch ---------------------------------------
*.pixproj

# ---- Project documentation kept private (S19), narrowed per Q-3 ------------
# docs/ holds the project's own documentation. It is PRIVATE BY DEFAULT (S19):
# a newly added doc file stays untracked unless someone deliberately widens
# one of the re-inclusions below. Q-3 (user decision, 2026-08-01) re-includes
# ONLY the lean slice needed to keep working on another machine from GitHub:
#   - docs/adr/   the architecture-decision-record trail.
#   - docs/site/  the mkdocs subtree CI builds (see .github/workflows/ci.yml,
#                 step "Docs build (mkdocs --strict, F14)": `mkdocs build -f
#                 docs/site/mkdocs.yml --strict`; its nav/docs_dir resolve
#                 entirely under docs/site/, so nothing outside this subtree
#                 is required to build it).
# Everything else under docs/ (CHANGELOG.md, module-map.md,
# deployment-sync-backend.md, packaging-native-installers.md, web-viewer.md,
# perf/) stays ignored/private.
#
# Mechanism: `docs/*` ignores docs/ contents one level deep (it does NOT
# ignore "docs" itself, so git still descends into it and evaluates the
# patterns below). Git will not apply a negation to a path whose own parent
# directory entry is still excluded, so each re-included subtree must be
# un-excluded at its OWN directory line -- here that is a single level
# (docs/adr, docs/site), so no further per-level cascade is needed beneath
# them; nothing re-excludes their contents, so everything below each
# un-excluded directory becomes visible to git automatically.
docs/*
!docs/adr/
!docs/site/

# Third re-inclusion (user decision Q-20): docs/constitution-articles.md is a
# GENERATED, REDACTED EXTRACT of the project constitution -- which itself
# lives outside this repository by a non-scopable layout invariant and was
# purged from git history -- published here so that the ~299 `Article <N>
# §<n>` citations carried by 45 ADRs and the phase specs resolve from a fresh
# clone. Regenerated by a container-level script; it is NOT hand-edited, and
# hand edits are detected and rejected. A SINGLE FILE is re-included, not the
# whole tree, so this narrows nothing else already private under docs/*
# (docs/CHANGELOG.md, docs/module-map.md, etc. stay ignored, same as today).
!docs/constitution-articles.md

# mkdocs' own build OUTPUT directory (mkdocs build -f docs/site/mkdocs.yml
# --strict writes here). docs/site/ is re-included above for its SOURCE
# (nav config + docs_dir pages) so CI/local runs can build it -- the
# generated HTML/CSS/JS this produces is a local artifact, never a checked-in
# one, so it needs its own exclusion beneath that re-inclusion.
docs/site/_build/
